 ### [PlaceTreeCone](5090-placetreecone.md)
-PlaceTreeCone generates a procedural voxel tree consisting of a trunk and a leaf canopy shaped as a truncated cone. It places wood blocks for the trunk and leaf blocks in a conical shape, respecting chunk boundaries. The method is distinguished by two documented implementations: a radial gradient with a circular cross-section check, and a fixed Manhattan distance heuristic for the canopy shape. Choose this when an organic, tapered look is desired. It differs from PlaceTreeBox by having a curved canopy profile [G]. [PlaceTreeCone](5090-placetreecone.md)
