 ### PlaceTreeBall
-PlaceTreeBall generates a tree with a spherical leaf canopy by checking the squared Euclidean distance from the center of the leaf volume [S4, unofficial]. It is distinguished by its use of a sphere shape, providing a more uniform, bushy appearance. Choose this for stylized or low-poly trees. It differs from PlaceTreeCone by having a constant radius canopy rather than a tapered one [G].
+PlaceTreeBall generates a tree with a spherical leaf canopy by checking the squared Euclidean distance from the center of the leaf volume [S4, unofficial]. It is distinguished by its constant-radius spherical shape compared to the tapered cone of PlaceTreeCone [G]. When to choose it: Not given in the sources.
 
 ### PlaceTreeBox
-PlaceTreeBox generates a tree with a rectangular prism leaf canopy by iterating over a 3D box centered on the trunk and placing leaf blocks probabilistically [S4, unofficial]. It is distinguished by its simple, blocky shape which is computationally cheaper and easier to tune. Choose this for voxel-art styles where organic shapes are not required. It differs from PlaceTreeBall and PlaceTreeCone by lacking curvature [G].
+PlaceTreeBox generates a tree with a rectangular prism leaf canopy by iterating over a 3D box centered on the trunk and placing leaf blocks probabilistically [S4, unofficial]. It is distinguished by its simple, blocky shape compared to the curved profiles of PlaceTreeCone and PlaceTreeBall [G]. When to choose it: Not given in the sources.
 
